{"yam":[{"id":"yam","headword":"यम्","headword_slp1":"yam","senses_r":[{"n":1,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"यम् (औ, उ) यच्छति 1.\na. To stop,\ncease, end, refrain. (क) यमयति,\nयामयति 10.\na. To feed; to res-\ntrain.\nAct with ञा to seize, to go\nto; with उत्^1 to rise, to endeavour;\nwith नि^2 to remove, to observe a rite,\nto restrain; with सं^3 to associate with;\nwith वि^4 and आ to exercise.\nDepon.\nwith आ to put forth the hand\nor any limb; with उप^5 to marry, agree\nto, learn; with सं^6 to heap together.\n[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20200322. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/issues/202.\n[2] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20200322. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/issues/202.\n[3] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20200322. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/issues/202.\n[4] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20200322. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/issues/202.\n[5] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20200322. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/issues/202.\n[6] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20200322. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/issues/202."}]}]}],"yama":[{"id":"yama","headword":"यम","headword_slp1":"yama","senses_r":[{"n":1,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"यम (मः-मा-मं)\na. Twin; one of a pair.\nm. Yama, Pluto, the god of\nhell; penance; restraint, stop.\nf. (मी) The\nJumnā. n. A pair."}]}]},{"id":"yAma","headword":"याम","headword_slp1":"yAma","senses_r":[{"n":1,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"याम (मः-मा-मं)\na. Relating to\nYama.\nm. The eighth part of a day;\nforbearance; cessation."}]}]}],"yamaka":[{"id":"yamaka","headword":"यमक","headword_slp1":"yamaka","senses_r":[{"n":1,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"यमक (कः-का-कं)\na. Twin; fellow.\nm. A religious obligation or ob-\nservance.\nn. Alliteration, rhyme."}]}]}],"yamakalindi":[{"id":"yamakAlindI","headword":"यमकालिन्दी","headword_slp